claim.claim-text:
a substrate (234);
a first doped region (222) formed in the substrate, at a top surface of the substrate, the first doped region having an associated first contact (224) configured to receive a first voltage;
a second doped region (226) formed in the substrate, at the top surface of the substrate, the second doped region having an associated second contact (228) configured to receive a second voltage;
a first resettable doped region (238) formed in the substrate, at the top surface of the substrate, between the first doped region and the second doped region, the first resettable doped region having an associated first resettable contact (240) configured to receive a reset voltage or be set as an open circuit, the first resettable region providing a potential barrier in the photodiode without the use of a gate; and
a first light absorbing region (236) formed in the substrate, at the top surface of the substrate, between the first doped region and the first resettable doped region, the first light absorbing region configured to generate first electron-hole pairs in the substrate,
wherein first electron-hole pairs are generated in the substrate when the first resettable contact is set as an open circuit, and the first electron-hole pairs are removed from the substrate when the first resettable contact receives the reset voltage, and
wherein the first doped region is a p+ doped region, the second doped region is an n+ doped region, and the first resettable region is a p+ doped region.
